/E (To that end, Ikey spent a lot of his time in Yeshivat Moreshet Yerushalayim building consistent habits, staying on track, and doing what he needed to do in order to secure his future. That consistency would serve him well much later down the road, when, in applying to law school, he would need to study for months to take the LSATs. He also spent a lot of time learning with Rabbi Gold, which he remembered enjoying a lot. )
